-- title:
--   Mennicke: Γ(m) inside commutator subgroup joined with Q_m
-- statement:
--   Let $m$ and $q$ be natural numbers, with $q$ nonzero (a `NeZero q` instance), and suppose $m$ and $q$ are coprime. Write $R =$ [`Ihara.ZAway q`](def/Gamma0Away.html#L11) for the localisation of $\mathbb{Z}$ away from $q$, i.e. $\mathbb{Z}[1/q]$, and work in the group $\mathrm{SL}(2,R)$. The subgroup [`Ihara.principalCongruenceAway m q hmq`](def/IharaMennickeCarrier.html#L42) is the kernel of the homomorphism $\mathrm{SL}(2,R) \to \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z}/m)$ obtained by applying, entrywise, the ring map $R \to \mathbb{Z}/m$ that exists because $q$ is invertible modulo $m$; thus it is the principal congruence subgroup of level $m$. The subgroup [`Ihara.mennickeQ q m`](def/IharaMennickeCarrier.html#L115) is the normal closure in $\mathrm{SL}(2,R)$ of the single element $A^m$, where $A$ is the image under $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z}) \to \mathrm{SL}(2,R)$ of the matrix $\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\1&1\end{pmatrix}$. The assertion is the inclusion of subgroups $$\Gamma(m) \le [\mathrm{SL}(2,R),\mathrm{SL}(2,R)] \vee \langle\!\langle A^m\rangle\!\rangle,$$ where $\vee$ denotes the join (the subgroup generated by the union) of the commutator subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}(2,R)$ and [`Ihara.mennickeQ q m`](def/IharaMennickeCarrier.html#L115).
--
--   This is Mennicke's inclusion from his work on Ihara's modular group: every matrix congruent to the identity modulo $m$ is, modulo commutators, a product of conjugates of $A^m$; equivalently the image of $\Gamma(m)$ in the abelianisation of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}[1/q])$ lies in the image of $Q_m$. It feeds the congruence-subgroup input of the Ihara-type analysis, being used in [`Ihara.gamma0Away_hom_factor`](thm.html#Ihara.gamma0Away_hom_factor) and [`Ihara.mennickeCSP_of_prime`](thm.html#Ihara.mennickeCSP_of_prime).
